# strand-eval reference recordings (docs/eval.md, "Reference recordings"). Written by `strand-eval approve` and `verdict`; a block edited by hand fails its seal.
ref "stagger-plain-turn"
verdict good
note "New regression (stagger review), restructured so each batch runs to its rest. Read with explain: into the shown bar the plain #plain, #nest and #head are at rest from their first frame and take no turn; the keyed rows and #preset (popin 0.8) start at 0, 40, 80 and 120 ms (#preset let go at k8, due 120 ms); the later batch's #latebox starts at its first frame k22 beside the plain #plainlate, at rest there; #cutbox's enter is cut by a mark on its first frame k36 and plays on (opacity 0.14, 0.39, ...); vanish passes it (the old pop-in rest read k36 as its own rest)."
